This README file contains a brief description of the verification case.

A simple test for a 1mm x 1mm x 1mm case with:

Temperature: 1273.15K
density: 1.0 g/cm³
fast neutron flux: 7.5e18 n/m²/s
fluxConversionFactor:0.85
stress:50 MPa

The calculated K = 8.53178680E-29
So the creep_rate = K*stress*flux*fluxConversionFactor = 2.7195070425E-08 /s
creep_strain at 7.5e6s = 0.2039630281875

The average creep_strain obtained by OFFBEAT is 0.203943762, the relative error is 0.00944592148450278%


The verification of creep in form of creep_rate = K * (sigma1 - vc*(sigma2+sigma3)) * phi 
as well as the solution for principal stress can refer to the case_4b of the Iaea_Benchamark
